From c3bfe325f85535c93b27efb3a7be23acce48bd81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Albin=20S=C3=B6derqvist?= <albin@albinutils.se>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:09:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rtc: pcf85063: force 24-hour mode when setting time
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The driver writes tm_hour as BCD using the Linux 0 to 23 hour range and
reads the Hours register as a 24-hour value. However, set_time() leaves
the 12_24 bit in Control_1 unchanged.

If the RTC is configured for 12-hour mode, set_time() can therefore
write a 24-hour encoded value while the hardware interprets the Hours
register using 12-hour format.

While stopping the RTC for the time update, also clear 12_24 and
EXT_TEST. This selects 24-hour mode and ensures that the hardware
interprets the hour value in the same format used by the driver.

Fixes: 31d4d33ef431 ("rtc: pcf85063: fix time/date setting")
Assisted-by: ChatGPT.6-Sol
Signed-off-by: Albin Söderqvist albin@albinutils.se
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf85063.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf85063.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf85063.c
index 2b4921c23467..01002f2a4c4b 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf85063.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf85063.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 
 #define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1		0x00 /* status */
 #define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_CAP_SEL	BIT(0)
+#define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_12_24	BIT(1)
 #define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_STOP		BIT(5)
 #define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_EXT_TEST	BIT(7)
 #define PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_SWR		0x58
@@ -120,7 +121,8 @@ static int pcf85063_rtc_set_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 	 */
 	rc = regmap_update_bits(pcf85063->regmap, PCF85063_REG_CTRL1,
 				PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_EXT_TEST |
-				PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_STOP,
+				PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_STOP |
+				PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_12_24,
 				PCF85063_REG_CTRL1_STOP);
 	if (rc)
 		return rc;
-- 
